From 9028f45108df24cadf9e877ffd26648da5ba1157 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(design): ship the theme module as TypeScript, one
 chooseTheme, no Secure

The package exports src/theme.ts as it is, so the compiled js/, its tsconfig, its
build step and the ignores for it go. writeTheme and applyTheme, always called
together, become chooseTheme; themeBoot() becomes the constant THEME_BOOT; the
theme names are written once. The cookie drops Secure, so a site served over
plain http shares the choice too (it carries no authority), and loses the try
blocks around document.cookie, which throws only in a sandboxed frame. The
theme-color metas, which followed the system and not the choice, are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tKeE4iJ874reAvf4rR
